pra: 0165 - praexecskip also matches the vnode name; the churners die on every exec path

ring22 (the 0164 boot, furthest ever: launchd spawning daemons, Setup
exec'd, sampler ran, zero card-busy) measured praexecskip working on
the namei path - locationd/WirelessRadioManagerd/CommCenter got 1-5
execs, launchd gives up - but bluetoothd/fairplayd.H2/
nanotimekitcompaniond churned 615/617/607 execs each, re-reading their
Mach-Os over single-sector PIO in the middle of Setup's page-in. Their
execs COMPLETE (the "exec %s" line prints from the allowed-spawn path),
so the 0147 hook misses whatever name they arrive with.

The hook now ALSO matches imgp->ip_vp->v_name (vnode_internal.h is
already in kern_exec.c's include set; every exec has ip_vp since the
image is read from it), so the skip fires regardless of which name
source the spawn path carries. Blocks print one line per name (capped
at 16, with the matched source: ndp or vp) - the next ring shows the
mechanism, never a flood.

migration + CommCenter from the donor's v12 ladder are already done
and measured working (datamigrator: 0 execs; CommCenter: 1). With the
churners blocked, Setup finally gets the IO and CPU the churn was
stealing.

---
 bsd/kern/kern_exec.c | 3 hunks
---
diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
index 5af697b..ee9d620 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -1166,9 +1166,10 @@ SYSCTL_PROC(_vm, OID_AUTO, shared_region_control,
  * such daemons accounted for 630 execs and most of the 3 GiB read.
  */
 static int
-pra_exec_skipped(const char *path)
+pra_exec_skipped(const char *path, const char *src)
 {
 	static int logged;
+	static int logged_blocks;
 	char list[256];
 	const char *base = path;
 	char *item, *comma;
@@ -1190,6 +1191,14 @@ pra_exec_skipped(const char *path)
 		comma = strchr(item, ',');
 		len = comma ? (size_t)(comma - item) : strlen(item);
 		if (len && strlen(base) == len && strncmp(base, item, len) == 0) {
+			/* 0165: ring22 measured launchd respawn-failing the same
+			 * daemons 600+ times per boot (bluetoothd, fairplayd.H2,
+			 * nanotimekitcompaniond), so each block decision is worth
+			 * a line - one per name, never a flood. */
+			if (logged_blocks < 16) {
+				logged_blocks++;
+				printf("praexecskip: blocked %s (%s)\n", base, src);
+			}
 			return 1;
 		}
 		if (!comma) {
@@ -1223,8 +1232,18 @@ exec_mach_imgact(struct image_params *imgp)
 	char *                  userspace_coredump_name = NULL;
 
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_PRA)
-	if (imgp->ip_ndp != NULL &&
-	    pra_exec_skipped(imgp->ip_ndp->ni_cnd.cn_nameptr)) {
+	/* 0165: ring22 measured the skip working for daemons exec'd on the
+	 * namei path (locationd, WirelessRadioManagerd, CommCenter: 1-5 execs,
+	 * launchd gives up) but bluetoothd/fairplayd.H2/nanotimekitcompaniond
+	 * churned ~600 execs each - their execs complete, so the hook misses
+	 * whatever name they arrive with. Match the vnode's component name
+	 * too: every exec has ip_vp (the image is read from it below), and
+	 * v_name is its last component (vnode_internal.h is already in the
+	 * include set). */
+	if ((imgp->ip_ndp != NULL &&
+	    pra_exec_skipped(imgp->ip_ndp->ni_cnd.cn_nameptr, "ndp")) ||
+	    (imgp->ip_vp != NULLVP && imgp->ip_vp->v_name != NULL &&
+	    pra_exec_skipped(imgp->ip_vp->v_name, "vp"))) {
 		error = EPERM;
 		goto bad;
 	}
